1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Meet FixQuest AI. Turn everyday home problems into interactive repair adventures. This recording uses an Amazon Fire tablet.

2
00:00:10,199 --> 00:00:18,199
Three rooms, three quests: a dripping tap, a slow sink, and a sticking door. Every action works with directional controls.

3
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:26,340
Start with a model tap. Observe the scenario, consider the clues, and learn when to stop for qualified help.

4
00:00:26,477 --> 00:00:33,477
The focus ring shows the selected answer. Use the D-pad to move and Select to make a choice.

5
00:00:33,622 --> 00:00:41,622
A wrong answer is a chance to learn. The guide gives a contextual nudge, and you can try again.

6
00:00:42,044 --> 00:00:50,044
QuestGuide offers curated guidance offline. It is deterministic, not live generative AI. Prompts can use an installed offline system voice.

7
00:00:50,431 --> 00:00:56,431
First, identify where the drip appears. Observation comes before guessing at a hidden problem.

8
00:00:56,631 --> 00:01:02,631
The model explains a likely cause, while recognising that different tap designs use different parts.

9
00:01:02,734 --> 00:01:10,734
Original illustrations and a simple toolkit make each decision visual. Here, choose a fitted spanner with a protective cloth.

10
00:01:10,941 --> 00:01:18,941
Now build a safe sequence in the model: isolate the water, verify flow has stopped, then replace the matching washer.

11
00:01:19,196 --> 00:01:25,196
The puzzle rewards the order of the checks. If isolation is uncertain, stop and get help.

12
00:01:25,424 --> 00:01:35,424
Mission complete. Earn a badge and experience points. The best completed result is saved locally, and retries remain part of learning.

13
00:01:36,016 --> 00:01:44,016
Another room brings another interaction. Align the virtual door marker with its target. This is a simulation, not a diagnosis.

14
00:01:45,912 --> 00:01:53,912
Small remote movements bring the model into alignment. The explanation reminds us that real doors can stick for several reasons.

15
00:01:54,092 --> 00:02:02,092
Knowing when a problem needs professional assessment is part of the game. Complete a quest to unlock its badge.

16
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:12,230
XP and badges stay on this device. Replaying can improve a best score, without counting the same mission again and again.

17
00:02:12,364 --> 00:02:20,364
No login, backend, or API key. FixQuest AI makes home knowledge a shared adventure. Fire TV demo footage is still required.
